  m_text: "Deer are hoofed ruminant ungulates belonging to the family Cervidae, characterized
    by their specialized digestive systems and the presence of antlers in most males
    (and both sexes in reindeer).  With 43 recognized species, they are native to
    all continents except Antarctica and Australia, inhabiting diverse environments
    ranging from tundra and taiga to tropical rainforests and savannas. \r\n\r\n"
