  m_text: Chickens (Gallus gallus domesticus) are domesticated birds descended from
    the red junglefowl of Southeast Asia, originally domesticated around 8,000 years
    ago.  With a global population exceeding 26.5 billion, they are the most widespread
    domesticated animal, primarily raised for meat and eggs.
