  m_text: The coconut palm (Cocos nucifera) is a vital tropical palm tree found along
    coastal areas worldwide, known as the "tree of life" for its immense utility
    in food, drink, and shelter. Growing up to \(30\text{m}\) (\(100\text{ft}\))
    tall, it produces fruits all year round and can live for 100 years, with major
    cultivation in Asia and the Pacific
