  m_text: A rose tree (or tree rose) is not a naturally occurring tree species, but
    rather a rose bush grafted onto a straight, tall stem to mimic a tree-like, single-stemmed
    shape. These artificial "standards" raise the rose blooms closer to eye level,
    providing a striking, elegant focal point for gardens and containers
