      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The tamarillo (Solanum betaceum), often called a tree tomato, is a small,
    fast-growing subtropical tree native to South America. It produces egg-shaped,
    edible fruits with a savory-sweet, tangy flavor similar to a mix of kiwi, guava,
    and tomato. These 10\u201318 foot trees thrive in warmer climates, have shallow
    roots, and are highly productive (over 40 lbs per tree)."
